Theorem L-10: Dimension extension requires per-rule proofs

  Preconditions:
    - Adding a new dimension D to the AimsState product lattice per
      Annex E §AIMS.8 L-10
    - The extension MUST preserve the prior axioms L-1 through L-8
    - L-10 is the META-THEOREM governing future lattice extensions;
      it does NOT add a new dimension itself — it constrains the
      addition protocol

  Soundness property:
    Forall new dimension D added to AimsState, the extended product
    lattice AimsState' = AimsState x D satisfies all of L-1..L-8 iff
    D satisfies the following four obligations:
      (a) D has finite height (re-prove L-5 for D);
      (b) D has a defined join operation dim_join_D : D x D -> D;
      (c) canonicalization extends to cover D's interaction with prior
          dimensions (CN-N rules updated if D introduces new feasibility
          constraints);
      (d) L-1 through L-8 still hold for the extended product (per-dim
          obligations + product-lift lemmas).

  Proof obligation:
    L-10 is a meta-theorem; the proof is a constructive schema that,
    given any candidate dimension D, exhibits the per-axiom obligations
    the addition must discharge.

    The proof is the discharge SCHEMA, not a particular dimension's
    discharge. It states: if D satisfies (a) + (b) + (c) + (d), then
    AimsState x D satisfies L-1 through L-8. The converse is also
    true by construction (the product-lift lemmas require per-dim
    versions of each axiom).

    Schema discharge by per-axiom componentwise-lift lemma:

      L-1' (extended commutativity):
        join_AimsState'((a, d1), (b, d2))
          = (join_AimsState(a, b), dim_join_D(d1, d2)) (def)
          = (join_AimsState(b, a), dim_join_D(d2, d1)) (L-1 + D-commut)
          = join_AimsState'((b, d2), (a, d1)) (def reverse)
        Holds iff (a) dim_join_D is commutative AND (b) AimsState has L-1.
        Existing AimsState has L-1 by sec-02 L-1 discharge; D-commut is
        obligation (d) component.

      L-2' (extended associativity): analogous — per-dim L-2 on D +
        product-lift implies extended product L-2.

      L-3' (extended idempotence): analogous — per-dim L-3 on D +
        product-lift implies extended product L-3.

      L-4' (extended partial order): the partial order on AimsState' is
        componentwise; (a, d1) le' (b, d2) iff a le b AND d1 le_D d2.
        Reflexivity / antisymmetry / transitivity at the product level
        follow from per-dim versions for all dims including D.

      L-5' (extended finite height):
        height(AimsState') = height(AimsState) + height(D) = 16 + h(D)
        Finite iff h(D) finite (obligation (a)).

      L-6' (extended transfer monotonicity): per-TF-N rule on the
        extended product is monotone iff (i) the rule's restriction
        to AimsState is monotone (already proven at sec-04) AND (ii)
        the rule's restriction to D is monotone (D-side obligation;
        a new TF-N variant per existing rule may be required if D
        introduces D-affecting transfer semantics).

      L-7' (extended canonicalization idempotence): canonicalize'
        composes existing CN-1..CN-8 with any new CN-* rules added
        for D (obligation (c)). Each new CN-* rule's idempotence is
        a per-rule obligation; composition idempotence follows from
        per-rule idempotence + fixpoint argument (analogous to L-7
        layer (a)).

      L-8' (extended canonicalization preserves joins): analogous —
        per-CN-rule (existing + D's new rules) preserve canonical form
        on canonical inputs; lifts to extended product.

    Worked example (illustrative; NOT a discharge of any specific D):
      Suppose D = ThreadShared = {Local, Shared}, height 1, join = max.
      Obligations:
        (a) height(ThreadShared) = 1; finite. PASS.
        (b) dim_join_ThreadShared = max on {Local, Shared}. defined.
        (c) Add CN-* rule if ThreadShared interacts with existing dims;
            e.g., CN-9 might say "Locality = top implies ThreadShared
            = Shared" (mirroring CN-6's wide-locality demotion). Verify
            CN-9 is idempotent + monotone + preserves canonical-form
            via per-pair enumeration on the relevant slice.
        (d) Apply schema lemmas above; sec-02 L-1..L-8 lift directly
            via componentwise extension.
      Result: AimsState' = AimsState x ThreadShared satisfies L-1
      through L-8.

    Removal direction:
      L-10 also constrains dimension REMOVAL (or merger). Removing D
      from AimsState produces AimsState'' = AimsState minus D; the
      axioms transfer trivially (dropping a dimension reduces the
      product-tuple length; per-dim axioms on the remaining dimensions
      are unchanged). Schema: for any d-slice to remove, verify the
      remaining product still satisfies L-1..L-8 (mechanically true if
      they held on the full product). Per HISTORY notes in
      Annex E §AIMS, the removal protocol is what landed CN-4 and
      CN-7's removal — both shown to be redundant (subsumed by other
      rules) without violating L-1..L-8.

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (schema verification per
        section_02::verify_l10_dimension_extension_schema)
      monotonicity (validates the L-6' lift — per-dim monotonicity on
        D implies product monotonicity on AimsState x D)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-10 as a meta-theorem schema; per-D obligations (a)+(b)+(c)+(d) are enumerated and the L-1'..L-8' lift lemmas constructed
